  "functions": [
    "FUNC.DECIMAL"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DECIMAL strips leading whitespace only, treats empty text as 0, and rejects trailing whitespace, signs, or radix outside 2..36",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, DECIMAL(text, radix) truncates radix to an integer in [2, 36] (#NUM! outside), trims leading whitespace only (so \"  10\" with radix 2 is 2 while trailing whitespace such as \"10\\t\" is #NUM!), returns 0 for empty text \"\", parses ASCII digits 0-9 and case-insensitive letters A-Z up to u128 capacity, and rejects signs or fractional separators with #NUM!. Matches 1,230/1,230 full-bank and 120/120 pinned DECIMAL rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (1,230/1,230 full-bank and 120/120 pinned DECIMAL rows in witnesses/DECIMAL.json) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 65).",
